---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';
const app = appBySlug('smsbump')!;
const path = '/apps/smsbump';
const title = 'SMSBump: retired sending and legacy record recovery';
const desc = 'Use the historical SMSBump identity to reconcile sending numbers, permissions and replacement records, rather than shortlist a new sender.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">App procurement directory</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Unranked operating guide · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>The sending service has been decommissioned</h2>
    <p>The <a class="link" href="https://smsbump.com/get-started">SMSBump lifecycle notice</a> states that Yotpo SMS has been decommissioned and that its dashboard and associated background services are no longer active. This is direct service evidence, beyond an unavailable app listing.</p>
    <p><a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/yotpo-smsbump-bringing-the-power-of-yotpos-platform-to-sms/">Yotpo’s product history</a> connects SMSBump to Yotpo SMS &amp; Email. The <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">migration announcement</a> scheduled full messaging deprecation for December 31, 2025. Treat SMSBump and Yotpo messaging as related historical identities, not two independent current candidates.</p>
    <h2>Start from records already held</h2>
    <p>Locate prior exports, invoices, account notices, sending-number records and destination import logs. Do not plan around logging into the retired dashboard. If records are missing, ask support what recovery remains possible and document the answer; the public notice does not promise an archive export or a recovery deadline.</p>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Reconcile against</th><th>Open issue to resolve</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Phone and customer identifiers</td><td>Destination profiles and Shopify customer identifiers</td><td>Normalization, duplicates and unmatched records</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Permission and opt-out history</td><td>Destination eligibility and suppression imports</td><td>Missing capture evidence or a status changed during import</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sending number and keywords</td><td>Provider confirmation and destination configuration</td><td>Ownership, transfer outcome and reply routing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Active forms and old links</td><td>Current storefront and landing-page configuration</td><td>Capture still pointing to an inactive service</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Campaign reports and invoices</td><td>Archived attribution definitions and final billing</td><td>Reporting gaps and unresolved charges</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>Prove suppression continuity before sending</h2>
    <p>Compare source and destination totals by channel status, then investigate each unmatched or unexpectedly eligible record. A total contact count can remain unchanged while opt-outs become subscribed. Preserve the original file and transformation rules so the reconciliation can be reproduced.</p>
    <p>Separate uncertain permission from known permission; do not fill missing evidence with a subscribed default. Use controlled test records to confirm that an imported opt-out remains excluded when a campaign audience is built. Check email preferences separately rather than assuming an SMS status supplies an email instruction.</p>
    <h2>Recover the sending identity deliberately</h2>
    <p>A saved number in an export does not prove the replacement provider can use it. Ask the providers to confirm ownership, transfer or replacement status, registration requirements and the receiving endpoint for replies. Record where STOP and HELP are handled for the active identity.</p>
    <p>Review old keyword ads, QR codes, packaging and signup links. Remove or replace routes that still point to retired capture. Confirm a new signup reaches the active sender with its source and disclosure evidence. Where an old keyword cannot be preserved, update the customer-facing instruction rather than treating it as a working path.</p>
    <h2>Repair an incomplete move</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>List every replacement flow and its intended customer event. Identify any still depending on a retired SMSBump callback or template variable.</li>
      <li>Rebuild required triggers and purchase exits in the destination. Check that delayed imports do not enroll historical contacts into a live welcome or cart flow.</li>
      <li>Exercise a test order, a channel opt-out and an expired offer. Save destination queue and suppression evidence.</li>
      <li>Remove obsolete storefront capture and integrations only after confirming their replacements and recording the change owner.</li>
      <li>Archive the final reconciliation, unresolved records and billing closure separately from new campaign reporting.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>This is a proposed recovery exercise, not a completed migration test. Mark unavailable source evidence explicitly; a destination rehearsal cannot reconstruct an unknown historical disclosure.</p>
    <h2>Keep historical reporting interpretable</h2>
    <p>Retain report date ranges, attribution windows, currency, refunds and message charges beside old totals. A new sender’s attributed revenue is not directly comparable if its definitions changed. Establish a new measurement baseline and assess eligible audiences and contribution after costs before scaling.</p>
    <h2>Catalog acceptance brief</h2>
    <p>{app.shopifyFit}</p>
    <p><strong>Can we restart SMSBump sending?</strong> The current lifecycle notice says its dashboard and background services are inactive. Procure a supported replacement and verify account recovery questions with support.</p>
    <p><strong>Must other Yotpo products be removed?</strong> Treat that as a separate dependency decision. The <a class="link" href="/apps/yotpo-email-sms">Yotpo migration review</a> covers retained Reviews and Loyalty integrations; this page owns SMS sending and record continuity.</p>
    <p>Use the <a class="link" href="/apps">app directory</a> for replacement acceptance briefs and the <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">consent guide</a> to define evidence requirements. Preserve a handover record with the new sending owner, suppression exceptions and number-transfer outcome.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
